// PARAM: --analysis interval,congruence
// Concretely the loop leaves x == 10: it starts at 4 and steps by 2 while
// x < 10. So 10 <= x holds and the branch on x == 11 is never taken.
//
// Neither analysis alone gets both. Interval bounds x to [10,11] after the
// loop, which proves 10 <= x but admits 11, so --analysis interval enters the
// branch and reports its check REFUTED. Congruence keeps x even, so the guard
// x == 11 leaves it no value and --analysis congruence reports the check DEAD,
// but it has no bounds and leaves 10 <= x UNKNOWN.
//
// Run together, each check is decided by the met answer, so Interval's proves
// the first; and the combined state is unreachable as soon as one active
// analysis's part is, so Congruence's dead branch is dead for both.
fun main() {
  x = 4;
  while (x < 10) {
    x = x + 2;
  }
  __voblint_check(10 <= x); // PROVED
  if (x == 11) {
    __voblint_check(x == 12); // NOWARN
  }
}
